#+BEGIN_SRC fish

cd $r/campapk/stage3

mkdir -p res/layout

#+END_SRC

Create the following activity_main.xml: 

#+BEGIN_SRC xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LinearLayout
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:gravity="center"
    android:padding="24dp">

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/message"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:text="Hello from layout.xml!"
        android:textSize="24sp" />

    <Button
        android:id="@+id/button"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:text="Press me" />

</LinearLayout>

#+END_SRC

Now we have to process it. Execute the following command from the
stage3 folder.

#+BEGIN_SRC fish
mkdir -p res-compiled linked gen

"$ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/34.0.0/aapt2" compile \
  res/layout/activity_main.xml \
  -o res-compiled/

#+END_SRC

This creates a file called layout_activity_main.xml.flat in the res-compiled
folder. It is a binary file, whose octal dump shows the content of activity_main.xml.

AAPT2's compilation and linking stages are deliberately separate:
compilation transforms the individual resource; linking combines
resources and assigns their resource IDs. 

Now we shall again invoke aapt2, but this time for linking:

#+BEGIN_SRC fish
"$ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/34.0.0/aapt2" link \
  -o linked/base.apk \
  --manifest AndroidManifest.xml \
  -I "$ANDROID_HOME/platforms/android-35/android.jar" \
  --min-sdk-version 23 \
  --target-sdk-version 35 \
  --java gen \
  res-compiled/layout_activity_main.xml.flat

#+END_SRC 

The "--java gen" line causes aapt2 to create R.java inside gen folder.

Also update our MainActiity.java:

#+BEGIN_SRC java

package com.example.helloworld;

import android.app.Activity;
import android.os.Bundle;

public class MainActivity extends Activity {

    @Override
    protected void onCreate(Bundle savedInstanceState) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState);

        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main);
    }
}
#+END_SRC

We now compile it with:
#+BEGIN_SRC fish
javac -d out \
    -cp "$ANDROID_HOME/platforms/android-35/android.jar" \
    gen/com/example/helloworld/R.java \
    src/com/example/helloworld/MainActivity.java
#+END_SRC
I guess just adding "gen" to the classpath would also work
(instead of asking explicitly to compile
gen/com/example/helloworld/R.java)
 
