* Suggested debugging routine for your manual build
Whenever a layout behaves unexpectedly, use this sequence:
1. Inspect the source XML. Check the parent and child attributes.
2. Recompile and relink. Make sure your APK includes the latest XML.
3. Run aapt2 dump xmltree. Verify that the intended attributes
   and values reached the APK.
#+BEGIN_SRC fish
aapt2 dump xmltree linked/base.apk \
  --file res/layout/activity_main.xml
#+END_SRC
4. Run aapt2 dump resources. Verify resource references and IDs
   if necessary.
#+BEGIN_SRC fish
aapt2 dump resources linked/base.apk
#+END_SRC
5. Install the rebuilt APK and inspect the running hierarchy. Check actual bounds and visibility.



Change one attribute at a time. Rebuild and compare the results.

